' =====================================================================
' RoboFetch - Scenario 2 of 3: an order is REFUSED because the robot
' could not get back to its station afterwards.
'
' The point of this scenario is the GATE ORDER. The four physical
' checks run first and the classifier is gate 5, so a refusal on the
' reserve returns before the model is ever asked - the AI service
' lifeline stays empty on purpose. A classifier can refuse an order
' the physics allowed; it can never approve one the physics rejected.
'
' Nothing is written and nothing is published, so a refusal costs one
' preview and there is nothing to undo.
' =====================================================================
@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #34495E
  LifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
  ParticipantBorderColor #34495E
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FBFCFE
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #EAF2FA
}

actor Controller as C
participant "Web tier" as API
database "SQLite" as DB
participant "AI service" as AI
participant "Task manager" as TM

== Cost the job ==
C -> API ++ : POST /preview  SKU-3001 -> delivery_1
API -> DB ++ : product, pick point, bay
DB --> API -- : 4.5 kg, pick (2.75, -1.5), bay (-3.0, -2.2)
API -> DB ++ : live robot condition
DB --> API -- : battery 80%, 41 C, condition 99%
API -> API : project past work already accepted, then cost\nthree legs: 8.63 m loaded + 3.00 m home\n= 6.54 + 1.12 Wh = 69.6 points of an 11 Wh pack

== Run the gates in order ==
API -> API : gate 1  stock: 1 in stock, passes
API -> API : gate 2  reserve: 80 - 69.6 = 10%,\nbelow the 15% that must remain
API --> C -- : REFUSED\n"battery would fall to 10%, below the 15%\nreserve needed to return to the station"

note over AI, TM
  Gate 2 returns immediately, so gates 3 to 5 never run: the classifier is
  not consulted and the task manager is never told. A refusal costs one
  preview, and there is nothing to roll back because nothing was written.
end note

@enduml
